On Saturday 15 November 2003 21:49 Yashichi wrote:

> If I want to inscribe a scroll or spellbook, what determines whether a
> spell is known or unknown? Must I have already read/memorized it from
> a book, or is merely having read a scroll (or even identifying one)
> enough?

If you've read or identified a scroll, you can write the scroll; if
you've read or identified a spellbook, you can write the spellbook. 

(meaning that you can't, for instance, write scrolls of identify if you
know *only* the identify spell and have never seen a scroll)

You always have a chance to write an unknown scroll or spellbook,
depending on your level and luck; for W that can get as high as 99%.

